I tried one of the sample codes (offboard_control) and in that i tried to display angular velocity data but i was getting zero. I also tried the IMU data but it again showed zero. 
 Telemetry::AngularVelocityBody v;
Telemetry::IMUReadingNED acc;
When i use mavros  and run the px4.launch file, then i can subscribe to the /imu/data topic and see the orientation and stuff but not without it.

```cpp
Telemetry::IMUReadingNED IMU;
std::cout<<telemetry->health()<<std::endl; 
int i = 1;
while (i>0)
{
    std::cout<<" acceleration is (down) "<<IMU.acceleration.down_m_s2<<std::endl;
    sleep_for(milliseconds(100));
}
```

This is the piece of code that I added in the takeoff_and_land.cpp example code to see the IMU readings.

@deepak-1530 you are printing an uninitialised struct.

You should do something like this:

```
while (true)
{
    Telemetry::IMUReadingNED imu = telemetry->imu_reading_ned();
    std::cout<<" acceleration is (down) "<<imu.acceleration.down_m_s2<<std::endl;
    sleep_for(milliseconds(100));
}
```

For more examples, see:
https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/develop/src/integration_tests/telemetry_sync.cpp

